From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:07:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/9] yblod-55: dvbridge: remove the video packing and film
 metadata paths

Since the Vulkan engine renders all video (yblod-30), tools/dvbridge only
packs and serializes graphics-only frames (the menu output):

- dvbridge_gl_pack() (packing a PQ video texture), the packer's IPT
  offset (dvbridge_gl_packer_set_ipt_offset, always zero) and the
  shader's video branch have no caller; the menu packing is unchanged,
  bit for bit (the offset was 0, the graphics branch is what remains);
- dvbridge_active_area() has no caller, and with it the L5 scan in
  dvbridge_prepare;
- dvbridge_prepare is only fed the one synthetic L1 block of
  dvbridge_prepare_graphics, so the serializer's L2, stream L5, L6 and
  CM4 branches never ran: it now takes exactly that L1 block (and adds
  the full-raster L5 as before), and mpv_dvbridge_cm4.h goes;
- the standalone-project scaffolding in tools/dvbridge/CMakeLists.txt.

Checked with git grep over the whole tree, the render code included.
